<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:40:04Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Transgressive, edgy DIY: What the 90s meant for British art</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c852dbb9c31b74a36ad52d42b58c5810c18594514fd6f2be341fadbcf38ac698</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:39:19Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T15:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/transgressive-edgy-diy-what-the-90s-meant-for-british-art/a-79581777--be96a24bef33.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/transgressive-edgy-diy-what-the-90s-meant-for-british-art/a-79581777?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 1990s are remembered for Britpop and provocative fashion, but beyond the nostalgia, it was a decade of cultural experimentation and social change. Tate Britain's new exhibition looks past the familiar icons.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Merz rails against extremism, AfD sympathizers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:76e9740ee202a0d1cb0edd8dcd7bd67b89612d142a37460a569077e270d95277</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:39:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T15:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-rails-against-extremism-afd-sympathizers/live-79570924--74b91e3a40aa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-rails-against-extremism-afd-sympathizers/live-79570924?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Political extremism threatens Germany's existing social order, Chancellor Merz has said. The Transport Ministry has proposed a five-year plan to improve Germany's ailing railroad infrastructure. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU enlargement: European Commission tables reforms to prepare bloc for new members</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b471e4357cd1db59dec20a05340e8a6d2a73a2393bc23eedd0e3d298456fce99</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:39:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T15:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-enlargement-european-commission-tables-reforms-to-prepare-bloc-for-new-members/a-79582493--0237e634d1b1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-enlargement-european-commission-tables-reforms-to-prepare-bloc-for-new-members/a-79582493?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Commission is proposing earlier access to EU markets for candidate countries, new voting rules to reduce vetoes and extra safeguards for a bigger bloc. But is the reform fair — or even feasible?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Why music in Iran is more than just entertainment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5e26882e5e3c2a6f56c2d65a8edfa7632a8504584041958db4b3ec7fbf731ba1</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:39:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T14:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-music-in-iran-is-more-than-just-entertainment/a-79583224--67cbee1305a2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-music-in-iran-is-more-than-just-entertainment/a-79583224?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iranian authorities are trying to persuade prominent singers in exile to return home. While the state seeks to harness music as a political tool, music has also become a powerful expression of dissent and resistance.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Sudan's road to elections remains uncertain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e239bcfef86ba68eb571181ce3d8b6b5ffa9add58080eff212e83473cfa117a9</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:39:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T13:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-sudan-s-road-to-elections-remains-uncertain/a-79563442--6016ef79f3a9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-sudan-s-road-to-elections-remains-uncertain/a-79563442?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">South Sudan's first general election is set for December 22. Insecurity, political tensions and failure to begin voter registration have raised doubts over whether the poll can be held credibly.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>China's Golden Week reveals cautious consumer spending despite travel surge</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5e57accb775201438113d08fcfca095e2c994d6844607ed325e44afd744498a9</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:39:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T13:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-s-golden-week-reveals-cautious-consumer-spending-despite-travel-surge/a-79577254--362469c231fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-s-golden-week-reveals-cautious-consumer-spending-despite-travel-surge/a-79577254?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chinese visitors are returning from trips after the 13-day Golden Week holiday. Their subdued spending has raised fresh questions about domestic demand in the world's second-largest economy.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>German spy scandal threatens national security</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a1de5813df3a03568a67bf1755db193dc08d463a44972556b39eb4d9ec6c059b</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:39:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T12:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-spy-scandal-threatens-national-security/a-79580000--1e3ca23b32e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-spy-scandal-threatens-national-security/a-79580000?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The arrest of Germany's former intelligence chief August Hanning could undermine national security, experts warn, as allies may reconsider their intelligence relationships.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>France suspends use of stun grenades against protesters</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9bba529a7e182d8f60c2c55ab3eb15b01881625ee020929140b39c6f053855ea</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:39:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T12:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-suspends-use-of-stun-grenades-against-protesters/a-79577769--d0b3dc0a1c76.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-suspends-use-of-stun-grenades-against-protesters/a-79577769?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">France is suspending the use of stun grenades against protesters as allegations of student brutality draw more anger. French Prime Minister Sebastien Lecornu is scheduled to address protesters later today.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Ex-spy chief sent to pretrial detention on treason charges</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bb0c41e2f61f21510168e78f2b36a405454acecc0d8221429a2f3abb85b9483e</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:39:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T11:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-ex-spy-chief-sent-to-pretrial-detention-on-treason-charges/a-79576300--68ee19fee871.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-ex-spy-chief-sent-to-pretrial-detention-on-treason-charges/a-79576300?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">August Hanning has been remanded into pretrial detention after his arrest. The case has prompted calls for transparency when spies leave the government.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Did CDU lawmakers support the far-right AfD?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:102711f95fca8221d8cbd1a1abe2944a1c6bcb2eb5e05eebfc39bfca1d4201d4</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:39:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T11:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-did-cdu-lawmakers-support-the-far-right-afd/a-79577396--ed4eac4ecf1f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-did-cdu-lawmakers-support-the-far-right-afd/a-79577396?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Lawmakers of the center-right CDU may have voted for the far-right AfD candidate for parliamentary speaker in Saxony-Anhalt. Germany's Social Democrats warn of a "unique breach of taboos."</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Nobel Prize in Chemistry goes to Henri B. Kagan and Kenso Soai</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8243a4d0f200a5fa83bca6b0cdc72404f235191019d5a10d18850250d25db0f4</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:39:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T09:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nobel-prize-in-chemistry-goes-to-henri-b-kagan-and-kenso-soai/a-79573924--1eccf7a6b469.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nobel-prize-in-chemistry-goes-to-henri-b-kagan-and-kenso-soai/a-79573924?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Henri B. Kagan and Kenso Soai won the Nobel Prize in Chemistry for their groundbreaking discoveries related to the origin of chirality and life's building blocks.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Suspected pneumonic plague in Siberia: What we know about the disease</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6717c51eed4063d33da727ef41cc507b39465bac70566b1d94dd92b67e6f06fc</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:38:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T09:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/suspected-pneumonic-plague-in-siberia-what-we-know-about-the-disease/a-79547919--6c7e74a1d6ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/suspected-pneumonic-plague-in-siberia-what-we-know-about-the-disease/a-79547919?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After a worker at a Russian plague research institute in Siberia died October 2, 2026, nearly 200 of her contacts were under medical observation. But authorities there denied pneumonic plague had caused the death.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ronaldo stays on under cloud as Messi exits internationals</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fa35ff1db04c3617808026fc2ada6b31e82651b67e7b9500a23736c5481d67c2</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:39:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T09:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ronaldo-stays-on-under-cloud-as-messi-exits-internationals/a-79574551--518c4a71824f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ronaldo-stays-on-under-cloud-as-messi-exits-internationals/a-79574551?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Just hours before Lionel Messi played his last match for Argentina, Cristiano Ronaldo posted his latest salvo in a row with Portugal. Ronaldo wants to play on despite the troubles, while Messi bathed in adulation.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Nobelitis — How winning a Nobel Prize can give you delusions of grandeur</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aca3ff0e368d217abb3acee7403f1f3b9c34533a3dabf81175b61e52ea383fd9</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:39:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T08:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nobelitis-how-winning-a-nobel-prize-can-give-you-delusions-of-grandeur/a-79525772--1ee420badedc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nobelitis-how-winning-a-nobel-prize-can-give-you-delusions-of-grandeur/a-79525772?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After being chosen for one of the world's most prestigious awards, some Nobel laureates lose touch with reality and suddenly start spouting unscientific nonsense. They're afflicted by what some have called "Nobelitis."</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>The solar boom is rapidly transforming emerging economies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:732b349f6d0eaf0bfb87f8a3f9e1f7dfebba70cbbe26f338d2d84fcd2b94d6ce</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:39:58Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T07:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-solar-boom-is-rapidly-transforming-emerging-economies/a-79474847--4010881b7e37.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-solar-boom-is-rapidly-transforming-emerging-economies/a-79474847?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Renewable electricity is cheaper than ever. While the West got rich on coal and oil, some of the world's poorest countries are banking on solar, wind and water instead.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Israel marks third anniversary of October 7 Hamas terror attacks with memorials</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:28c567e9762025299df11e08426252f50aca5508b00d6eb97ebd119987677448</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:40:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T06:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/israel-marks-third-anniversary-of-october-7-hamas-terror-attacks-with-memorials/a-79571380--52f2728d0d00.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/israel-marks-third-anniversary-of-october-7-hamas-terror-attacks-with-memorials/a-79571380?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Families gathered at the Nova music festival site and other attack locations in memory of those killed by Hamas-led attacks on October 7, 2023.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen's Houthis claim strikes on Aden, Riyadh airports</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:424ddb087e65d5e42f1f7f6b52b6da39065528ab15341bd198cd2423b64358fa</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:40:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T06:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/yemen-s-houthis-claim-strikes-on-aden-riyadh-airports/a-79571321--0245466ede4d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/yemen-s-houthis-claim-strikes-on-aden-riyadh-airports/a-79571321?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Aden International Airport came under attack as Yemen's war intensified, with the Houthis targeting key transport hubs. Around 200,000 people have been displaced by the fighting between government forces and the Houthis.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Opposition protest clouds Modi's 25-year milestone</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2ff9f57c36612dd2afd755519d041c6c1f4386677082951329429b5e1131e677</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:38:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T05:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-opposition-protest-clouds-modi-s-25-year-milestone/live-79570653--dd5c6b9365a9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-opposition-protest-clouds-modi-s-25-year-milestone/live-79570653?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Delhi police has beefed up security around the Election Commission of India, likely preparing for another day of 'vote theft' protests. Meanwhile, PM Modi marks 25 years in public service.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Where is Spain headed after the snap election announcement?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9b6ffe71211f488bdb6a07e8287ca509c00fa5ef4fb3bad2fb8190f7fe4e8cb4</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:38:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T04:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/where-is-spain-headed-after-the-snap-election-announcement/a-79567959--1490181fc735.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/where-is-spain-headed-after-the-snap-election-announcement/a-79567959?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez is taking a gamble by calling an early election in Spain. The housing crisis, migration and the rise of the right-wing populist Vox party are all likely to dominate the campaign.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Mali: Junta forces retake strategic town of Kidal from separatists</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2eebff7b8ba08c6dec95ea3fa213649be4b33058fffd9aa36893f6be772fadd9</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:38:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T02:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/mali-junta-forces-retake-strategic-town-of-kidal-from-separatists/a-79570617--dc7ca7f76853.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/mali-junta-forces-retake-strategic-town-of-kidal-from-separatists/a-79570617?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Mali's military regained control of the strategic town of Kidal after forcing Tuareg separatists and al Qaeda-linked jihadists to withdraw following an offensive backed by Russia's Africa Corps.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Football: Lionel Messi plays final game for Argentina</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:97c64b6915f478ec296d51d7bec20215cee1d5a21eec9ce71d0205613500509c</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:38:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T02:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/football-lionel-messi-plays-final-game-for-argentina/a-79570608--6687ff69f964.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/football-lionel-messi-plays-final-game-for-argentina/a-79570608?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Argentinian superstar Lionel Messi bowed out of international football with one last goal for his country. For football in Argentina, and indeed across the world, it's the end of an era.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
